{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01, which implements a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand what needs to be done:\n\n1. For each call, compute `normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens`\n2. A call is accepted if `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n3. Return `accepted_call_ids` (list of accepted call IDs) and `diagnostics` (list with `call_id`, `normalized_gain`, `accepted` for each call in original order)\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: gain = (1.94835097 - 0.38569502) / 5 = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = (1.06116273 - 0.68319969) / 4 = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = (1.21810502 - 0.47260371) / 6 = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = (1.05721833 - 0.29767903) / 5 = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.1519079 (actually 0.75953930/5=0.15190786), parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = (1.06717367 - 0.85733566) / 5 = 0.20983801 / 5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → gain \u003c 0.05, NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = (1.66191711 - 0.89798497) / 4 = 0.76393214 / 4 = 0.19098304, parseable=true → accepted\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out what rounding to use. Let me look at the schema - `normalized_gain` is a `number` type. The artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify precision. I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, maybe 8 decimal places, or perhaps I should not round at all. Let me re-read.\n\n\"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - This is vague. Let me just use standard Python float arithmetic without explicit rounding, or perhaps round to 8 decimal places.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, I think I should just compute the float value and not do explicit rounding - the \"rounded\" might just mean the natural float representation. Let me implement without explicit rounding since the schema just says `\"type\": \"number\"`.\n\nNow let me write the `solve(case)` function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        normalized_gain = (loss_without - loss_with) / prediction_tokens\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me validate the field requirements:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings ✓\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `call_id`, `normalized_gain`, `accepted` ✓\n- Order preserved ✓\n- No mutation of input ✓\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON object with key \"implementation\" where the value is the Python source code as a JSON string.\n\nLet me write the final response properly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id must be a string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_without_call must be a number for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"loss_with_call must be a number for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, int) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer for call {call_id}\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"parseable must be a boolean for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        normalized_gain = (loss_without - loss_with) / prediction_tokens\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01NBActTSNx7qqWMJ7KTbTRd","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2470,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":49,"output_tokens":1571,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1089},"service_tier":"standard"}}